### On MGMT02
Enable RDP on mgmt02
Go to Settings -> System -> Remote Desktop -> Enable Remote Desktop

Create the DMZ->LAN and LAN->MGMT rules necessary for RDP to connect to mgmt02
On edge01:
  set firewall ipv4 name DMZ-to-LAN rule 20 action accept
  set firewall ipv4 name DMZ-to-LAN rule 20 description 'Allow RDP to mgmt02'
  set firewall ipv4 name DMZ-to-LAN rule 20 destination address '172.16.200.11'
  set firewall ipv4 name DMZ-to-LAN rule 20 destination port '3389'
  set firewall ipv4 name DMZ-to-LAN rule 20 protocol 'tcp'
  commit
  save

On fw-mgmt:
  set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-MGMT rule 40 action accept
  set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-MGMT rule 40 description 'Allow RDP to mgmt02'
  set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-MGMT rule 40 protocol tcp
  set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-MGMT rule 40 source address '172.16.50.4'
  set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-MGMT rule 40 destination address '172.16.200.11'
  set firewall ipv4 name LAN-to-MGMT rule 40 destination port '3389'
  commit
  save

Invoke an SSH connection from traveler to jump so that RDP connections in that tunnel are redirected to mgmt02.

ssh -i $env:USERPROFILE\.ssh\id_rsa -p 2222 -L 13389:172.16.200.11:3389 jump-azrael-passless@10.0.17.120

This creates a tunnel where:
- Local port 3389 on Traveler gets forwarded through jump to mgmt02 at 172.16.200.11:3389

RDP through the tunnel
On Traveler open Remote Desktop Connection and connect to:
127.0.0.1:13389
